From: AX6 local correctness review <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nss: include the common header in received status length

cm.len excludes the common header while skb->len includes all received
bytes. Compare the full declared message against the aggregate active
length, for both linear and assembled status frames. Header availability
is checked before this point. Keep existing table isolation, ordinary
dispatch, alignment and owner routing unchanged.

This is not a per-type minimum-length check or a contiguous-range fix.
Do not infer a firmware size limit, stop/drain or DMA retirement policy.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -435,7 +435,7 @@ static void nss_core_handle_nss_status_pkt(struct nss_ctx_instance *nss_ctx,
 	/*
 	 * Validate message size
 	 */
-	if (header.len > nbuf->len) {
+	if (nss_cmn_get_msg_len(&header) > nbuf->len) {
 		nss_warning("%px: Message %d for interface %d received with invalid length %d, expected length %d",
 							nss_ctx, header.type, nss_if, nbuf->len, header.len);
 		return;
